{
  "baseRefOid": "3c7b455eec27c436f76f08ed28efb30135c86f4f",
  "body": "The corrected expert-scale image gate passes on all three TP3 ranks: 132 files, 7,337 passed, 355 skipped, zero failures or errors per rank. The completed initial primary preserves all 256 recorded generated sequences and 65,536 returned score vectors exactly.\n\nRetain 114 lossless archives with original byte lengths and SHA-256 identities: all native gate reports, the complete primary, model comparison, operator launch error, actual controller exit and C36 restoration receipt. That primary used the newer stream collector. Its deliberate handoff stops before companions/repeat/functional checks, so this PR claims no matched serving improvement or release qualification. The distinct recorded-collector cohort remains separate.\n\nValidation: all 150 archive length/hash checks; `bin/spark doctor`; both isolated arms' complete `build check`; `git diff --check`. Runtime source, serving image, configuration and immutable baselines are unchanged.\n\nRetain 36 additional archives of the existing October 30 first/repeat performance inputs. The repeat covers decode, companions, mixed stalls and three common prefill sizes; no compatible 524288/1000000 reference repeat is invented. Document the published long-prefill extension\u2019s identity/condition limits and C36\u2019s newer collector plus missing repeat. GitHub validation jobs are configured as skipped; the local checks above ran.\n",
